            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0653" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851B.20/137: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General in Martinique (Malige) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort-de-France</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-12T18:00:00-04:00">November 12,
                            1942—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>488. From Reber. My 481, November 11. I called on Robert today to inquire what
                    effect Pétain’s declaration concerning the Armistice published yesterday would
                    have upon the status of these Colonies.</p>
                <p>Robert admitted he had little information as to the situation in France but in
                    the absence of specific directives insists that no change in his relations with
                    “his Government” is contemplated, that only the territorial clauses of the
                    Armistice have been affected. He wishes to <pb facs="0654" n="648"
                        xml:id="pg648"/> maintain his communications with Vichy and will still
                    consider that he needs to give the Germans advance notice regarding the
                    movements of his ships. It is obvious that he desires to make as little change
                    in the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> as possible and will take no
                    action that might appear contrary to whatever attitude may be adopted by Pétain.
                    He is waiting further clarification before finally determining his position.
                    [Reber.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Malige</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
